BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Liars in Paradise
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T220000
UID:bm-5891020260804@shop.queenbooks.ca
DESCRIPTION:[In Store]\nJoin us for the launch of\nLiars in Paradise\nby O
 lesya Lyunza\, and a conversation moderated by Nekesa Afia! Meet the autho
 r\, mingle\, and get your book signed.\nRSVP for free entry here!\nOlesya 
 Lyuzna\nis a historical fiction writer with a passion for queer noir. Her 
 debut novel\nGlitter in the Dark\nwas selected for a 2020 Pitch Wars mento
 rship by Layne Fargo and Halley Sutton. She lives in Toronto and spends he
 r free time hosting murder mystery parties and scouring the archives for u
 nsolved crimes.\nBorn in Calgary but now residing in Toronto\,\nNekesa Afi
 a\nholds a degree in journalism from Toronto Metropolitan University and a
  certificate in publishing from Centennial College.\n\nA self-proclaimed m
 idcentury-modern fan\, Nekesa loves a Saturday afternoon spent in front of
  the classic movie channel. When she isn’t writing\, you can find her se
 wing\, swing dancing\, or actively trying to pet every dog she sees.\n\nNe
 kesa Afia is also the author of the Harlem Renaissance Mystery series.
LOCATION:914 Queen Street East
URL:https://shop.queenbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Queen Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Becoming: A Writing Social on Liminality\, Self-Return & the Futur
 e Self (Workshop)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260820T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260820T203000
UID:bm-5891220260820@shop.queenbooks.ca
DESCRIPTION:[Off-site]\nDive into writing\, explore your future self\, and
  vibe with others on that in-between\, transformative energy.\nBecoming\ni
 s a grant-funded\, grassroots literary event exploring life’s in-between
  seasons through poetry\, author readings\, guided writing\, wellness\, an
 d Korean-inspired future-self letter writing.\nCreated by Ese (IG: @esewri
 tes_)\, Becoming is the third event in an ongoing Writing Social series in
 spired by the stages and themes of her manuscript-in-progress\, which refl
 ects on her time in East Asia and her re-entry into Toronto after five yea
 rs abroad.\nThis gathering explores liminality — the transitional season
 s where we are no longer who we once were\, but not quite where we hope to
  be. Attendees are invited to slow down\, connect\, and reflect on who the
 y are becoming.\nSupported by community grant funding\, Becoming hopes to 
 help build a longstanding community of writers\, readers\, and creatives a
 cross Ontario. It offers a warm and intimate space for anyone navigating c
 hange\, seeking creative connection\, or longing to be reminded that they 
 are not alone in the in-between.\nRSVP here for free entry!
LOCATION:Typist Studios & Coffee - 390 Dupont St.
URL:https://shop.queenbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Queen Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Mystic and the Missing Girl
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T210000
UID:bm-5891320260825@shop.queenbooks.ca
DESCRIPTION:[Off-site]\nJoin us for the launch of\nThe Mystic and the Miss
 ing Girl\nby Vikki VanSickle at Black Lab Brewing! Meet the author\, mingl
 e\, and get your book signed.\nVikki Vansickle\nis the author of a number 
 of acclaimed novels for children including\nThe Lightning Circle\; Words T
 hat Start With B\; Summer Days\, Starry Nights\;\nthe award-winning\nThe W
 innowing\n\; and picture books\nHow to Decorate a Christmas Tree\; If I Ha
 d a Gryphon\; Teddy Bear of the Year\; Anonymouse\; and Into the Goblin Ma
 rket.\nVikki started her career as an independent bookseller and worked in
  children's publishing for twelve years. In addition to writing\, she cura
 tes and presents regular book segments for CTV's Your Morning. Currently\,
  she lives and writes in Toronto.\nThe Mystic and the Missing Girl\nis Vik
 ki’s adult fiction debut. You can find her on Instagram at @vikkivansick
 le.
LOCATION:Black Lab Brewing - 818 Eastern Ave
URL:https://shop.queenbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Queen Books
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
